From 39472ab4180eb7c1dedbea1bdd2c5b6c4455b4ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oussama Benjelloun <benje.oussama@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 15:13:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] HIP: device math library and wave32/wave64 warp shuffles

amdgpu_dev.ll provides the device-side math Halide expects (sqrt/floor/
ceil/trunc/round/abs via LLVM intrinsics; sin/cos/tan/exp/log/pow/atan2 and
the inverse/hyperbolic set as generated polynomial code with documented ulp
bounds; fast_inverse via rcp/rsq; trap) and __shfl_sync-style shuffle
helpers on ds_bpermute. LowerWarpShuffles now handles DeviceAPI::HIP with
the wavefront size derived from the target arch (64 on gfx9, 32 on gfx10+)
and emits the HIP helpers; CUDA lowering is unchanged. Adds a lowering test
and an error test for over-wide gpu_lanes loops.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
